# The Hero's burst button. For 20 seconds the Combo Counter is worth more,
# and every Raging Blow tears the space it swings through.
#
# The orb line reads as a fifth bargain per orb and is not one: it lifts what
# the orbs ALREADY grant by 13%, whichever skill pays it. GMS's own spec
# tables walk Combo Attack's 20 ATT to 22.2 and Advanced Combo's 120% final
# damage to 133.2%, which is that multiplier and nothing else.
#
# Two of GMS's three clauses are dropped. The orb charge rate it halves has
# nothing to bite on -- the ring is a static count here -- and Soul Trace
# fires off Spirit Calibur, a 6th job skill this game never reaches.
#
# GMS says only "periodically" and keeps the number in Skill.wz, but a 41
# second battle analysis settles it: 180 rifts over a 30 second window is 60
# firings, one every half second, which is exactly a Raging Blow. The tear
# rides the swing rather than a clock, so a faster Hero tears more often.
#
# That is 7,200% a firing against the swing's own 1,548%, and it is meant to
# be: the Hero is a burst job, hugely stronger with this up than without.
name: "Instinctual Combo"
description:
  "Tap into your subconscious abilities and use your power to its fullest "
  "potential. Increases the ability gained from the Combo Orb and allows you "
  "to leave a tear in space when Raging Blow is used. The tear in space is "
  "unaffected by attack reflection."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ACTIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_HERO_V skill_order: 3 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
base_delay_ms: 120
cooldown_seconds: 120.0
buff {
  duration_seconds: 20.0
  base { combo_orb_gain_pct: 0.043 }
  per_level { combo_orb_gain_pct: 0.003 }
  pulse {
    label: "Tear in Space"
    paced_by_skill_name: "Raging Blow"
    casts: 3
    lines: 6
    max_enemies: 6
    base { skill_pct: 1.97 }
    per_level { skill_pct: 0.07 }
  }
}
